  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 7.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.4,
      "end_seconds": 11.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.51,
      "end_seconds": 26.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.94,
      "text": "Right, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening. She's been having a milky discharge from my breasts, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.85,
      "end_seconds": 30.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.76,
      "end_seconds": 35.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "About three days, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 36.92,
      "end_seconds": 42.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer five days, um, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.25,
      "end_seconds": 48.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.88,
      "end_seconds": 52.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Yes, uh, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.54,
      "end_seconds": 58.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 58.95,
      "end_seconds": 64.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.19,
      "end_seconds": 68.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "So, later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.41,
      "end_seconds": 83.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "Oh, you know, and periods stopped for four months. Ah, and there's being told it was just stress as well, about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.94,
      "end_seconds": 88.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.79,
      "end_seconds": 94.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 95.35,
      "end_seconds": 102.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to tramadol once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.42,
      "end_seconds": 106.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.48,
      "end_seconds": 117.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Okay, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.86,
      "end_seconds": 123.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "I've had heart disease for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.33,
      "end_seconds": 129.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.19,
      "end_seconds": 134.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "I've had migraines for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.79,
      "end_seconds": 140.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.81,
      "end_seconds": 153.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "Mm, uh, I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent. I mean, I'm on propranolol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.01,
      "end_seconds": 157.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.68,
      "end_seconds": 162.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "40 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.85,
      "end_seconds": 163.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.08,
      "end_seconds": 168.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Sumatriptan I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.83,
      "end_seconds": 171.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.94,
      "end_seconds": 174.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.77,
      "end_seconds": 177.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Right, how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.36,
      "end_seconds": 183.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.02,
      "end_seconds": 202.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.67,
      "end_seconds": 207.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.28,
      "end_seconds": 225.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "What about weight change?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.38,
      "end_seconds": 230.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No weight change, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.58,
      "end_seconds": 236.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Any hot flushes, visual changes or positive pregnancy test?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.88,
      "end_seconds": 251.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "No, um, no hot flushes, no visual changes, no positive pregnancy test. I did have headaches at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.01,
      "end_seconds": 255.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.33,
      "end_seconds": 259.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.23,
      "end_seconds": 262.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.45,
      "end_seconds": 265.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 266.6,
      "end_seconds": 277.06,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 80 beats a minute, weight 66 kilos, height 155 centimetres. Saturation 97 percent, blood pressure 125 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.14,
      "end_seconds": 280.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.8,
      "end_seconds": 286.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.07,
      "end_seconds": 290.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.73,
      "end_seconds": 316.25,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "You are not pregnant by the urine test, the breasts express a little milk, and there is no visual field loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.95,
      "end_seconds": 317.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.31,
      "end_seconds": 345.34,
      "duration_seconds": 22.03,
      "text": "Right, that's all I needed to check. Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards raised prolactin or a thyroid problem rather than stress. I'd also keep pituitary tumour in mind. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had a milky discharge from your breasts, and no visual changes or positive pregnancy test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.41,
      "end_seconds": 348.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.55,
      "end_seconds": 369.52,
      "duration_seconds": 18.97,
      "text": "Don't stress about stress as the cause, the tests will tell us. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.38,
      "end_seconds": 374.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.21,
      "end_seconds": 376.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}